# TIBER-Harness environment (placeholder values only — never commit real keys).
#
# CI runs entirely on MockProvider and requires NONE of these.
# Remote providers are future follow-ups (see docs/PROVIDER_BOUNDARY.md) and are
# only ever constructed when their key is present in a local/operator environment.

# COHERE_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Local Ollama provider (opt-in, never used in CI) -----------------------
# `npm run eval:ollama` runs the existing fixtures through a locally running
# Ollama model. It pulls/installs nothing and uses no API keys. See
# docs/LOCAL_OLLAMA_PROVIDER.md.
#
# Loopback HTTP is still a network call, so the network opt-in is required:
# TIBER_HARNESS_ALLOW_NETWORK=1
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=
